{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again","id":1089277,"title":"Stone Scribes, again.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T11:35:22-07:00","id":1089277,"title":"Stone Scribes, again.","content":"Third time's the charm, right?<br /> <br /> What I'm thinking is that since it's Time primary what the Stone Scribes probably do is collect information about people, places and thing and then examine where those things intersect in Time in order to recover a Final Name by the &quot;hole&quot; left in history by a person's missing Final Name. If they have the person on hand, or a recent corpse it's pretty easy to reconstruct a Momentary or Final Name, but the legacy spends a lot of energy focusing on the lost Final Names because it hopes to find the Names of Mages from the Time Before.<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is, since Time only bothers to concern itself with the Sympathy of its subjects own past selves, can it be used to determine that for instance, &quot;Was this book was in this library at this time?&quot; if you're able to target the book and the library simultaneously? Or, &quot;Or was this shield and this sword were held by the same person at the same time.&quot; I think if it can, then Stone Scribes can work on recovering a Final Name by triangulating with as many pieces of intersecting paraphernalia as possible till they hit an information critical mass that results in the discovery of the Final Name.<br /> <br /> That's just the Time part, haven't figured out the Death bit.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:36:42-07:00","id":1089609,"title":"","content":"Oh this is why you were asking about how to do that in the Ask a Question thread. Anyways, to answer your question yes - I believe it's entirely possible to establish if two objects were connected around the same time - however after some thought, I think that it may (by default) require some kind of space component because technically both -did- or -may have- existed during the same time, the questions your asking are whether or not they existed in the same space through time. It's complex and original, but I do like this idea - and I think as far as attainments go, the need for space may not actually be required to learn the attainment - just to use it without the legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:19:32-07:00","id":1089620,"title":"","content":"I remember somewhere someone asking if having a modified Arcanum Attainment for a Legacy Attainment would be feasible. If the normal Temporal Sympathy rules don't permit what you want the Namers to do, then this is exactly the place to do this.<br /> <br /> On another note, the 2e intro on the Stone Scribes give Time as their Ruling Arcanum. In 1e however they had Fate, and this actually makes more sense with the revelation from Mummy crossover that name-magic is related to Fate. Is this something you'll address, or just leave it be as Weird Magic Shenanigans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:15:55-07:00","id":1089661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089620#post1089620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, the 2e intro on the Stone Scribes give Time as their Ruling Arcanum. In 1e however they had Fate, and this actually makes more sense with the revelation from Mummy crossover that <b>name-magic is related to Fate</b>. Is this something you'll address, or just leave it be as Weird Magic Shenanigans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I was leaning to Prime with this (and I think its still doable) but Im more than interested in this. Do you remember the page number?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:54:19-07:00","id":1089692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089620#post1089620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, the 2e intro on the Stone Scribes give Time as their Ruling Arcanum. In 1e however they had Fate, and this actually makes more sense with the revelation from Mummy crossover that name-magic is related to Fate. Is this something you'll address, or just leave it be as Weird Magic Shenanigans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan on sticking to Time if I can, for one it's the twin of Fate anyway, for two, I'm already playing a Stone Scribe in a game but the attainments are basically in flux until I feel like I've really nailed them and Time was the primary arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089609#post1089609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it may (by default) require some kind of space component because technically both -did- or -may have- existed during the same time, the questions your asking are whether or not they existed in the same space through time. It's complex and original, but I do like this idea - and I think as far as attainments go, the need for space may not actually be required to learn the attainment - just to use it without the legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I keep thinking, Space component to read Sympathy, but I don't expect to be using this kind of power on things that have much Sympathy to each other. Or Space to pinpoint a location in Space, but with Postcognition you could theoretically scrub backward and forward on its timeline, and apparently Postcognition doesn't have the viewing restrictions that Scrying does letting you &quot;witness events as if you were there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe what I should do is give them Postcognition, let them use it on multiple subjects at once, and the vision is only of events where all subjects were present (Assuming you declare the right date and time which means it's not a free info handout). This gives some versatility, you get regular postcog, because you don't -have- to cast on multiple subjects and typically Mages don't, but it also lets you eliminate non-related items from your searches. So you get your hands on a hero's sword, Postcognition, you notice a shield in the vision that also belonged to the owner of the sword and you go hunting for the shield. Eventually you find one, and then you use Postcognition again to verify that this is the very shield you saw with the sword. Then you can check its past and start a new treasure hunt all over again. Build up a big enough collection of this stuff and you can perform a ritual with a later attainment to recover a Final Name.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think that would work? It's basically just a fancy verification system for subject authenticity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-08-2017, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:25:28-07:00","id":1089765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089661#post1089661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice. I was leaning to Prime with this (and I think its still doable) but Im more than interested in this. Do you remember the page number?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm running on second-handed knowledge myself, since I don't yet have Dark Eras Companion. Sorry if I was misleading.<br /> <br /> I only heard people saying the stuff comes up in DEC, but before that Dave pretty much confirmed that the five Pillars correspond to the five Subtle Arcana. Which isn't completely new, since it goes back all the way up to how the soul was described to be made up of the five Subtle Arcana in the Left-Handed Path (or whatever book it was that the Tremere were detailed in)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of which, the correspondences are; Ab to Spirit, Ba to Mind, Ka to Prime, Ren to Fate, and Sheut to Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:45:21-07:00","id":1089775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089765#post1089765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I'm running on second-handed knowledge myself, since I don't yet have Dark Eras Companion. Sorry if I was misleading.<br /> <br /> I only heard people saying the stuff comes up in DEC, but before that Dave pretty much confirmed that the five Pillars correspond to the five Subtle Arcana. Which isn't completely new, since it goes back all the way up to how the soul was described to be made up of the five Subtle Arcana in the Left-Handed Path (or whatever book it was that the Tremere were detailed in)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of which, the correspondences are; Ab to Spirit, Ba to Mind, Ka to Prime, Ren to Fate, and Sheut to Death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have the book myself but haven't got time to properly digest it yet. Ren is a Names Pillar, right? I don't have mummy so I don't really know how 'names' work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:50:08-07:00","id":1089778,"title":"","content":"Back on topic please, I think I'm comfortable with using Postcognition modified with the ability to run a verification check.<br /> <br /> What about the other stuff a Stone Scribe is supposed to be able to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:53:19-07:00","id":1089780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089775#post1089775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have the book myself but haven't got time to properly digest it yet. Ren is a Names Pillar, right? I don't have mummy so I don't really know how 'names' work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, &quot;Ren&quot; means &quot;name.&quot; It goes down to the concept that a thing's name is a record of its nature, what is has done and what it is doing and what it will do. While Ka/Essence is the unchanging fundament of something's existence that shows Who and What You Are, Ren/Name is more like Big Data applied on that person's life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:54:50-07:00","id":1089781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089778#post1089778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic please, I think I'm comfortable with using Postcognition modified with the ability to run a verification check.<br /> <br /> What about the other stuff a Stone Scribe is supposed to be able to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantling. How would one accomplish that with 2e spells and rules? It's important enough to be included in the short description, and it was their peak Attainment in 1e right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:19:50-07:00","id":1089797,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I could see it two ways, a variant of Rewrite History, or let the Deatb Optional stuff handle that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:00:59-07:00","id":1089983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089692#post1089692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I keep thinking, Space component to read Sympathy, but I don't expect to be using this kind of power on things that have much Sympathy to each other. Or Space to pinpoint a location in Space, but with Postcognition you could theoretically scrub backward and forward on its timeline, and apparently Postcognition doesn't have the viewing restrictions that Scrying does letting you &quot;witness events as if you were there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe what I should do is give them Postcognition, let them use it on multiple subjects at once, and the vision is only of events where all subjects were present (Assuming you declare the right date and time which means it's not a free info handout). This gives some versatility, you get regular postcog, because you don't -have- to cast on multiple subjects and typically Mages don't, but it also lets you eliminate non-related items from your searches. So you get your hands on a hero's sword, Postcognition, you notice a shield in the vision that also belonged to the owner of the sword and you go hunting for the shield. Eventually you find one, and then you use Postcognition again to verify that this is the very shield you saw with the sword. Then you can check its past and start a new treasure hunt all over again. Build up a big enough collection of this stuff and you can perform a ritual with a later attainment to recover a Final Name.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think that would work? It's basically just a fancy verification system for subject authenticity.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> <br /> Well it's less about them having sympathy and more a question of if there ever -was- sympathy. That said, no I don't think that postcognition would really work by default. Not because it wouldn't work but... because it's kind of like watching the video of an entire objects life. Even running in fast forward, looking at 400 years of information is going to take -time-. Looking at an entire -year- is going to take time. If you knew the date that they were supposed to be together before hand it'd be more effective, but even still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:22:22-07:00","id":1089995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1089983#post1089983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'<br /> <br /> Well it's less about them having sympathy and more a question of if there ever -was- sympathy. That said, no I don't think that postcognition would really work by default. Not because it wouldn't work but... because it's kind of like watching the video of an entire objects life. Even running in fast forward, looking at 400 years of information is going to take -time-. Looking at an entire -year- is going to take time. If you knew the date that they were supposed to be together before hand it'd be more effective, but even still.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scrubbing Reach Option doesn't say how fast you can scrub backward and forward, and Duration sets the period of time that you can view so I assume you'd have to get up to Indefinite Duration to see a subject's entire past.<br /> <br /> Anyway, obviously you'd want to do some investigative legwork ahead of time in order to reduce your chances of guessing blindly.<br /> <br /> The way I see it right now, first you date a subject to know how long it's been around. Then you guess or investigate a likely time of importance in its history and use Postcognition to view that, and look for any other objects that stand out. Then you hunt for those other objects and use multiple subject Postcognition to run a verification check on if you are in fact managing to collect the genuine armaments of Achilles or whatever.<br /> <br /> The idea is that you collect these artifacts shooting for something that was present at the death of the person with the lost Final Name so you can then witness that death and procure the Final Name in the vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-08-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:29:30-07:00","id":1090050,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking the first attainment should be a sort of inverted Momentary Flux, where rather than giving you information about the future and whether a person will be beneficial to you it takes a glance at a subject's past and determines a brief general descriptor. So you use it on a woman passing by and Time turns up the most significant identity signifier from her Unchanged Past of Devoted Mother. This can serve as a Momentary Name, and then if it's done in their final moments can also signify their Final Name. I think the second attainment should then be a Knowing effect that allows you to determine time stamps for significant changes in their lives, for instance you know what the Devoted Mother's Unchanged Past is, but this attainment could tell you at what point she went from being Enthusiastic Partier to Devoted Mother, or Rambunctious Child to Enthusiastic Partier. That could be contested by Temporal Sympathy, but by Time 3 that wouldn't be much of an issue anymore. Then you throw in Postcognition using the added information from the second attainment as jumping off points to try and narrow the area in time in which the moments before death occurs so you can witness that and use the first attainment to get the Final Name. Obviously, need to work out the attainments, but how's that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T23:42:16-07:00","id":1090131,"title":"","content":"Complex, but could work. I'll have to reread the sympathy rules (and this thread) to get a hang of all this, though.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to how it all ends up, since I had Stone Scribes as one of my translation goals in my thread. (It's been pushed out of priority for now, but it's still in the roster somewhere)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T05:51:33-07:00","id":1090254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1090131#post1090131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complex, but could work. I'll have to reread the sympathy rules (and this thread) to get a hang of all this, though.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to how it all ends up, since I had Stone Scribes as one of my translation goals in my thread. (It's been pushed out of priority for now, but it's still in the roster somewhere)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically one step of info gathering building on another, refining or easing the process at each step. Then the 4th and 5th attainments could be using that Final Name. I figure Death should do a lot of the heavy lifting for the &quot;action&quot; part of the legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T18:41:57-07:00","id":1090548,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, I can probably merge my ideas for the first and second Time attainments, the first attainment is supposed to grab their Final Name, it isn't a stretch to assume that with Time 2 you could also grab Momentary Names that they used to have before growing into their Final Name. I think the second attainment would then be Postcognition, and the third would be Shield of Chronos with the +1 Reach to play a false history, in this case borrowing the history of Final or Momentary Names. The Fourth attainment could be Choose the Thread with Reach spent to also affect spell casting rolls, drawing on the experience of a Final Name rather than looking to the future (Would only work for casting if they have a Final Name belonging to a Mage with the appropriate arcana). Then the final Time attainment could be Rewrite History with Reach assigned to Instant and Advanced Duration to cloak themselves in borrowed pasts.<br /> <br /> Death stuff: First attainment modifies the first one so it also works on corpses. Pulling a blank on ideas for the next attainment, maybe it can be used in conjunction with the Postcognition to verify the time of death of anyone in the vision if they've died? The third attainment could be Suppress Aura, so they not only make their past difficult to detect because it's shrouded by the dead, but under that cloak they're protected from other methods of scrutiny as well. I'm tempted to make the fourth attainment Corpse Mask then, they damage themselves in a manner reminiscent of whatever killed the deceased whose Name they're using and appear to look like that person when they took their final breath, death wound and all. Obviously some disguises will work better than others, it'd be hard to explain why you look like the Headless Horseman at the moment. The last attainment could essentially let you be &quot;possessed&quot; by the Final Name, allowing you to draw on the skills, merits and attributes of the deceased (Basically an excuse to get the two +1 Reach clauses on Rewrite History).<br /> <br /> How's that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T08:41:31-08:00","id":1169640,"title":"","content":"If I treat Names as a Mystery that the first attainment allows you to perceive and Scrutinize with MS, what might be the best way to determine Opacity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T14:25:01-08:00","id":1169730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1169640#post1169640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I treat Names as a Mystery that the first attainment allows you to perceive and Scrutinize with MS, what might be the best way to determine Opacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 for each level of sympathy away, between the Scribe and the deceased<br /> (Connected +0, Strong +1, etc)<br /> +1 for each level of Temporal sympathy away between the Name and its owner (Unchanged +0, Strong +1, etc)<br /> +1 for each dot of Occultation the owner had<br /> -1 for each dot of Fame the owner had<br /> Not sure if each dot of Gnosis higher than that of the Scribe should add to or subtract from Opacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:00:22-08:00","id":1169738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1089277-stone-scribes-again?p=1169730#post1169730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+1 for each level of sympathy away, between the Scribe and the deceased<br /> (Connected +0, Strong +1, etc)<br /> +1 for each level of Temporal sympathy away between the Name and its owner (Unchanged +0, Strong +1, etc)<br /> +1 for each dot of Occultation the owner had<br /> -1 for each dot of Fame the owner had<br /> Not sure if each dot of Gnosis higher than that of the Scribe should add to or subtract from Opacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, seems like the Opacity might jump up sharply if you don\u2019t know your subject very well and time passed. I think if I\u2019m doing the math right you could be looking at Opacity 11 if you don\u2019t know the subject very well and they\u2019ve been dead a long time with Occultation 3. That seems high to me, but I feel like it\u2019s on the right track.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019d drop the increase in Opacity from lack of Sympathy to the subject. That would bring maximum Opacity down to a more reasonable 7. The only problem is that I think it would put getting Momentary Names at Opacity 0. Maybe the living should get Opacity from a Resistance Attribute?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-22-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T08:58:30-08:00","id":1169936,"title":"","content":"Just realized setting Opacity by temporal sympathy doesn't really work either since what you dig up is either a Momentary Name (So Unchanged) or a Final Name (The point of which is that it doesn't change, so Unchanged).<br /> <br /> So the best I can think of is to set a base Opacity of 2, +1 if you don't know the subject's Sympathetic Name, +X from Occultation, and CoW against powers that deliberately obfuscate identities.<br /> <br /> This makes regular people rather easy to decipher, but makes the more powerful Mages that the legacy tries to dig up more difficult to puzzle out.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T09:28:32-08:00","id":1170198,"title":"","content":"Second attainments: Time 2, spend a scene studying a Name and gain the Informed Condition, no Beat on resolution. You can\u2019t have more than one instance of Informed running at a time. <br /> <br /> Death 2: Modified Speak with Dead: While you hold the Informed Condition you also know if the person with the Name left a ghost, where it can be found, can sense its Anchors and can see and speak with it regardless of communication barriers once the ghost is within Sensory Range.<br /> <br /> Thinking on 3rd attainment set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T11:41:32-08:00","id":1171010,"title":"","content":"For the 3rd attainment, ugh this has been hard, but I\u2019ve been toying with the idea of Shield of Chronos with the Reach clause granting a false timeline. Basically, you mantle yourself in a Name and can then spoof time investigations by running events from that Name\u2019s life. I\u2019m not sure how good that is though.<br /> <br /> For Death it would be Without a Trace, but you\u2019d also leave a false evidence trail instead of nothing at all that points at the original bearer of the Name. I could also see an argument for Suppress Aura that acts as an aid in being disguised as the original bearer of the Name, but that kind of subtle aura manipulation is probably more suited to Prime.<br /> <br /> Other thoughts, a variant of Divination geared toward getting specific answers on questions from a Name about the past of its original bearer, or just straight up use the Name as a substitute subject for Postcognition.<br /> <br /> No thoughts yet for the Optional Death attainment if I go that route.<br /> <br /> Does anyone at all have an idea or opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-28-2017, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T08:01:18-08:00","id":1172640,"title":"","content":"1st: Time 1: Use Scrutiny to obtain a Momentary Name<br /> Death 1: Use Scrutiny to obtain a Final Name from someone who has already passed.<br /> <br /> 2nd: Time: Use an effect like Divination with a scene long ritual of asking a Momentary or Final Name questions about its bearers past, Reach spent on getting more than yes or no answers.<br /> Death: Ritual activation Speak with Dead effect centered on the Stone Scribe with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and bypassing any language barriers. Dice penalties to Scale.<br /> <br /> 3rd: Time: Look at a Final or Momentary Name and gain the Informed Condition, no Beat on Resolution<br /> Death: Ghost Shield with ritual activation and Reach spent on Advanced Duration and protection from the physical attacks of ghosts.<br /> <br /> Apparently I'm stuck after that again, the final couple of attainments should more fully cover mantling yourself in a Name, but I'm not sure how to approach it yet.<br /> <br /> Ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T08:27:19-08:00","id":1176778,"title":"","content":"Okay, looked over the original Stone Scribes again, and I noticed the spell Analyse Final Name which provides varying levels of information at varying levels of success.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m contemplating using that as a model for setting Opacity for the Mage Sight modification for the first attainment. The first level of Opacity revealed the most basic information, who the person is, Virtue, Vice, and every level of Opacity after that also reveals something digging down to level 5 where you know everything there is to know about the bearer of the Name.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also thinking about gating attainment use behind those levels of Opacity, so for instance you can\u2019t use the second Attainment unless you\u2019ve drilled through two levels of the Name\u2019s Opacity. This might require some book keeping since you may have gotten through all 5 levels of Opacity for on Frank, but only 3 on Steve and this can\u2019t use the 4th or 5th attainments with Steve\u2019s Final Name.<br /> <br /> For the 4th attainment I\u2019m thinking of using a version of Temporal Summoning, a mirage of the bearer of the Final Name \u201creplacing\u201d the Stone Scribe. Not sure what to do with the Death part.<br /> <br /> Comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}